WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:01:52.130 --> 00:01:56.180
<b>Aqua Laguna</b>

3
00:02:07.020 --> 00:02:09.480
She jumped off the bridge!

4
00:02:15.070 --> 00:02:16.740
[PAULIE]
Don't follow her!

5
00:02:17.330 --> 00:02:18.580
[WORKMAN]
Paulie.

6
00:02:18.690 --> 00:02:21.230
[PAULIE]
You running down there isn't gonna do her
a lick of good.

7
00:02:21.260 --> 00:02:22.230
[WORKMAN]
But...

8
00:02:22.260 --> 00:02:24.600
You know how dangerous it is.

9
00:02:24.630 --> 00:02:26.530
You'll drown, just like her.

10
00:02:26.560 --> 00:02:28.830
If it gets bad, I'll
handle things, myself.

11
00:02:29.380 --> 00:02:31.150
I wouldn't have the guts to do that.

12
00:02:31.180 --> 00:02:32.750
She's either brave or stupid!

13
00:02:32.780 --> 00:02:35.220
No, this is definitely stupid!

14
00:02:35.220 --> 00:02:35.890
Hey!

15
00:02:35.890 --> 00:02:36.760
Come back!

16
00:02:36.780 --> 00:02:37.480
Quick!

17
00:02:37.480 --> 00:02:39.680
The sea's gonna swallow you up!

18
00:02:39.720 --> 00:02:41.720
[CHOPPER]
A sea anemone.

19
00:02:45.020 --> 00:02:47.270
A sea anemone?

20
00:02:47.720 --> 00:02:51.230
Why is a sea anemone coming out of a
chimney?

21
00:02:53.130 --> 00:02:55.260
Wait a second.

22
00:03:11.610 --> 00:03:12.310
No, wait!

23
00:03:12.310 --> 00:03:14.450
Not the reindeer, too!

24
00:03:14.480 --> 00:03:16.620
Zoro!

25
00:03:17.780 --> 00:03:18.500
I don't care who you're up
against. We'll help you!

26
00:03:18.500 --> 00:03:21.770
[CHIMNEY]
You're awesome, Pirate Lady!

27
00:03:21.800 --> 00:03:23.540
Don't be a fool, girl!

28
00:03:23.730 --> 00:03:26.020
You won't make it back in time!

29
00:03:26.140 --> 00:03:27.740
You can see for yourself!

30
00:03:27.780 --> 00:03:30.710
The wave's gonna
hit any second now!

31
00:03:33.390 --> 00:03:34.260
[WORKMAN]
Oh man!

32
00:03:34.290 --> 00:03:35.690
There's no turning back now!

33
00:03:35.730 --> 00:03:38.560
They're as good as dead!

34
00:03:40.610 --> 00:03:41.710
Zoro!

35
00:03:41.750 --> 00:03:42.720
Hey!

36
00:03:42.750 --> 00:03:44.720
You okay?

37
00:03:44.750 --> 00:03:46.380
Can you hear me?

38
00:03:46.420 --> 00:03:48.450
[ZORO]
Chopper?

39
00:03:52.170 --> 00:03:53.370
This is it.

40
00:03:53.400 --> 00:03:55.700
I can't go any further.

41
00:04:11.360 --> 00:04:12.230
You idiot!

42
00:04:12.260 --> 00:04:15.430
What the hell are
you doing up there?!

43
00:04:17.140 --> 00:04:18.340
[LUFFY]
Nami?

44
00:04:18.370 --> 00:04:19.340
Where are you?

45
00:04:19.370 --> 00:04:21.340
I can't see!

46
00:04:22.710 --> 00:04:25.740
Okay, listen, listen,
it's not my fault.

47
00:04:25.870 --> 00:04:28.440
That pigeon guy sent me
flying and I got stuck

48
00:04:28.470 --> 00:04:30.850
between these buildings,
so I can't move.

49
00:04:30.850 --> 00:04:32.980
I'm trying, though!

50
00:04:33.030 --> 00:04:37.030
[LUFFY grunting]

51
00:04:43.770 --> 00:04:45.270
Is this a joke to you?!

52
00:04:45.300 --> 00:04:47.070
We don't have time for this!

53
00:04:47.100 --> 00:04:49.640
Those guys from the
government took Robin away

54
00:04:49.670 --> 00:04:52.510
and you weren't
even there to help!

55
00:04:56.080 --> 00:04:58.750
She did it all for us, you know!

56
00:04:58.780 --> 00:05:01.580
She's going to
sacrifice herself!

57
00:05:11.040 --> 00:05:13.550
The government was
planning on attacking us,

58
00:05:13.580 --> 00:05:18.050
but Robin turned herself over
to CP9 so we would be safe!

59
00:05:18.080 --> 00:05:19.650
There's no place
left in this world

60
00:05:19.690 --> 00:05:21.860
for me to go, or return to.

61
00:05:21.890 --> 00:05:23.190
I'm afraid you're wrong.

62
00:05:23.220 --> 00:05:26.120
This is the last time you'll ever see me.

63
00:05:26.960 --> 00:05:31.300
[NAMI]
She knew they would kill
her but she didn't care!

64
00:05:34.370 --> 00:05:40.540
[LUFFY]
Then Robin was
lying this whole time?

65
00:05:46.610 --> 00:05:49.620
I'm glad.

66
00:05:52.460 --> 00:05:53.920
Don't worry!

67
00:05:55.380 --> 00:05:57.710
I won't let Robin die!

68
00:05:58.370 --> 00:05:59.810
[WORKMAN]
Check out the size of that thing!

69
00:05:59.840 --> 00:06:00.740
Oh man!

70
00:06:00.770 --> 00:06:03.380
The waves've never
been that big before!

71
00:06:03.410 --> 00:06:05.650
Hey this is really bad, guys!

72
00:06:05.680 --> 00:06:07.080
Run away, pirate lady!

73
00:06:07.110 --> 00:06:08.620
You gotta get out of there!

74
00:06:08.720 --> 00:06:10.020
You too, reindeer!

75
00:06:13.470 --> 00:06:15.410
[ZORO]
You're gonna tear me in half!

76
00:06:15.440 --> 00:06:17.110
[CHOPPER]
You're really stuck!

77
00:06:17.140 --> 00:06:20.180
How'd you get in
there in the first place?!

78
00:06:20.210 --> 00:06:21.550
Who cares?!

79
00:06:28.690 --> 00:06:30.120
What do we do?

80
00:06:30.160 --> 00:06:33.130
That wave's gonna hit any second now!

81
00:06:33.160 --> 00:06:36.230
[ZORO]
How the hell should I know?

82
00:06:36.280 --> 00:06:38.350
Ah Hold on that's funny.

83
00:06:38.390 --> 00:06:39.420
Hey Chopper.

84
00:06:39.450 --> 00:06:41.190
Are you carrying the Kintentsu?

85
00:06:41.190 --> 00:06:41.720
Huh?

86
00:06:41.720 --> 00:06:42.560
Your sword?

87
00:06:42.970 --> 00:06:44.340
Yeah, I have one of them.

88
00:06:44.570 --> 00:06:45.740
How on earth did you know that?

89
00:06:45.800 --> 00:06:49.730
Well, I can tell with that
one at least since it's cursed.

90
00:06:49.770 --> 00:06:52.800
Anyway, thanks for carrying it for me.

91
00:06:52.840 --> 00:06:53.600
Here, quick.

92
00:06:53.610 --> 00:06:55.310
Put it in my hand.

93
00:06:56.380 --> 00:06:57.250
Run away!

94
00:06:57.280 --> 00:07:01.080
Get to higher ground! Hurry!

95
00:07:01.120 --> 00:07:03.050
[WORKMAN]
It's all over, they're
not gonna make it!

96
00:07:03.060 --> 00:07:05.870
They'll get swept away for sure!

97
00:07:12.260 --> 00:07:14.500
Aqua Laguna is here!

98
00:07:25.270 --> 00:07:27.000
Oh no.

99
00:07:34.740 --> 00:07:36.580
They're done for!

100
00:08:00.670 --> 00:08:02.640
Whoa! That guy's
out of control!

101
00:08:02.670 --> 00:08:04.470
He's knocking over buildings!

102
00:08:15.170 --> 00:08:17.170
[ZORO]
Stay back, Chopper!

103
00:08:19.550 --> 00:08:24.480
One-Sword Style!
Thirty-Six Caliber Phoenix!

104
00:08:31.310 --> 00:08:32.160
[WORKMAN]
This is bad!

105
00:08:32.160 --> 00:08:33.530
They're wrecking the town!

106
00:08:35.430 --> 00:08:36.130
Nami!

107
00:08:36.170 --> 00:08:37.210
Let's go!

108
00:08:42.070 --> 00:08:43.340
Holy crap!

109
00:08:43.370 --> 00:08:44.310
[CHOPPER]
Rumble!

110
00:08:44.340 --> 00:08:46.610
Jumping Point!

111
00:08:46.760 --> 00:08:47.670
Just hold on to me!

112
00:08:54.340 --> 00:08:56.310
[WORKMAN]
They're washing away!

113
00:09:00.080 --> 00:09:01.240
[LUFFY]
Damn it.

114
00:09:13.020 --> 00:09:13.990
[WORKMAN]
Hey look!

115
00:09:16.560 --> 00:09:19.420
They made it, I think!

116
00:09:34.640 --> 00:09:35.440
Yay!

117
00:09:35.470 --> 00:09:37.180
You did it!

118
00:09:38.440 --> 00:09:40.150
They should be
safe on the bridge.

119
00:09:40.180 --> 00:09:42.850
Yeah. It's a big wave,
but it's not that big!

120
00:09:42.880 --> 00:09:44.620
You guys're amazing!

121
00:09:44.650 --> 00:09:46.680
You gotta teach me that one!

122
00:10:03.170 --> 00:10:05.170
Oh no, the tidal
wave's still coming!

123
00:10:05.200 --> 00:10:06.440
Did Straw Hat make it?

124
00:10:06.470 --> 00:10:15.080
I don't know, man,
all I can see is water!

125
00:10:15.110 --> 00:10:17.980
Look! Over there!

126
00:10:20.140 --> 00:10:21.680
It's Paulie!

127
00:10:28.460 --> 00:10:30.030
Crap.

128
00:10:45.880 --> 00:10:47.350
Hurry!

129
00:10:50.250 --> 00:10:51.840
We're not safe yet!

130
00:10:51.840 --> 00:10:54.050
Run to shipbuilding island!

131
00:10:56.800 --> 00:10:57.900
Run for it!

132
00:10:57.940 --> 00:10:59.800
The bridge is done for!

133
00:11:16.090 --> 00:11:18.840
[LUFFY ET AL. shouting]

134
00:11:31.170 --> 00:11:33.240
I've never seen
anything like that.

135
00:11:33.270 --> 00:11:35.370
The waves have never made it this far
before!

136
00:11:35.420 --> 00:11:38.220
I thought we'd be safe here!

137
00:11:38.220 --> 00:11:38.820
Look!

138
00:11:38.820 --> 00:11:40.090
The tide's ebbing again.

139
00:11:40.120 --> 00:11:41.120
Of course it is.

140
00:11:41.160 --> 00:11:42.860
This is just the beginning.

141
00:11:42.880 --> 00:11:44.050
There's gonna be
another wave like that

142
00:11:44.080 --> 00:11:45.890
and another after that one!

143
00:11:45.900 --> 00:11:47.170
If we wanna live, we gotta get

144
00:11:47.210 --> 00:11:49.880
to higher ground
like everyone else.

145
00:11:53.340 --> 00:11:57.340
[ZORO groaning]

146
00:12:00.520 --> 00:12:01.820
[PAULIE]
You morons.

147
00:12:01.870 --> 00:12:03.070
You're lucky you're alive.

148
00:12:03.100 --> 00:12:03.940
[LUFFY]
Thanks.

149
00:12:03.970 --> 00:12:06.310
You saved us, Rope Guy.

150
00:12:06.880 --> 00:12:09.850
[NAMI]
I didn't know Aqua Laguna
would be like that.

151
00:12:10.040 --> 00:12:11.920
I can't stop shaking!

152
00:12:13.500 --> 00:12:16.240
If it was that bad every year,
we'd be sunk.

153
00:12:16.270 --> 00:12:18.540
I'm just as surprised as you folks are.

154
00:12:18.540 --> 00:12:20.210
This ain't normal at all.

155
00:12:20.360 --> 00:12:23.330
[KOKORO]
You pirates are one
step shy of crazy!

156
00:12:23.360 --> 00:12:25.370
You're lucky to be alive right now.

157
00:12:25.370 --> 00:12:25.850
[LUFFY]
Oh!

158
00:12:25.850 --> 00:12:27.480
Hey, Monster Granny!

159
00:12:27.520 --> 00:12:29.950
I didn't know you were here too!

160
00:12:29.950 --> 00:12:31.390
Of course I am!

161
00:12:31.450 --> 00:12:32.650
I may be drunk,

162
00:12:32.690 --> 00:12:35.960
but I'd have to be stupid to
stay at sea during this storm!

163
00:12:36.600 --> 00:12:38.540
[CHIMNEY]
You were awesome, Mister Pirate!

164
00:12:38.570 --> 00:12:41.440
Your arms were
like "boing!" "boing!"

165
00:12:42.640 --> 00:12:47.180
Yeah, I know.

166
00:12:47.210 --> 00:12:48.410
I was gonna die!

167
00:12:50.180 --> 00:12:52.250
Little turd put my
face in a death grip

168
00:12:52.280 --> 00:12:54.280
then passed out like that.

169
00:12:55.530 --> 00:12:58.240
[LUFFY]
Hey, Zoro what were
you doing down there

170
00:12:58.270 --> 00:13:00.200
when the wave hit?

171
00:13:00.240 --> 00:13:01.610
Couldn't you get away?

172
00:13:01.640 --> 00:13:03.110
Oh, uh, yeah.

173
00:13:03.140 --> 00:13:04.080
You know.

174
00:13:04.140 --> 00:13:05.890
Zoro got stuck in a chimney.

175
00:13:06.520 --> 00:13:08.790
You got stuck in a chimney?

176
00:13:14.400 --> 00:13:16.400
Zoro, you dope!

177
00:13:16.590 --> 00:13:18.460
I couldn't be that lame if I tried!

178
00:13:18.490 --> 00:13:21.200
Don't forget, you did
the same thing... twice!

179
00:13:21.230 --> 00:13:23.200
You're both dopes, okay?!

180
00:13:23.230 --> 00:13:27.400
Wait where's Sanji
and U... Where's Sanji?

181
00:13:28.170 --> 00:13:31.200
Oh yeah, there's a lot of
stuff I need to tell you.

182
00:13:31.240 --> 00:13:32.710
You too, Zoro.

183
00:13:32.740 --> 00:13:35.080
[ZORO]
Hm?

184
00:13:40.130 --> 00:13:42.430
Things are certainly
looking up for me!

185
00:13:44.010 --> 00:13:46.510
[SPANDAM]
Aokiji is a generous man.

186
00:13:46.540 --> 00:13:48.670
Putting all those officers
and all those battleships

187
00:13:48.670 --> 00:13:51.040
at the tip of my fingers.

188
00:13:51.070 --> 00:13:53.140
Not that I haven't earned it, though.

189
00:13:53.170 --> 00:13:54.270
Under my fine leadership,

190
00:13:54.380 --> 00:13:59.190
CP9 has certainly accomplished
some excellent results.

191
00:13:59.520 --> 00:14:04.330
Now aren't you happy
for your master, Funkfreed?

192
00:14:04.360 --> 00:14:06.000
But no accolade is too great

193
00:14:06.030 --> 00:14:08.200
for the team who
captured Nico Robin.

194
00:14:08.230 --> 00:14:09.630
She's been a stain on the pride

195
00:14:09.660 --> 00:14:12.140
of the government
for 20 years now.

196
00:14:12.170 --> 00:14:14.140
And speaking of
stains, now that I know

197
00:14:14.170 --> 00:14:16.670
that detestable
Cutty Flam is still alive,

198
00:14:16.720 --> 00:14:20.020
I can have the satisfaction
of making him suffer.

199
00:14:20.060 --> 00:14:22.160
Only two people
in this wide world

200
00:14:22.190 --> 00:14:23.660
have the means
of reviving Pluton

201
00:14:23.690 --> 00:14:27.200
and both of have been
nicely gathered together.

202
00:14:27.230 --> 00:14:28.260
And let me tell you,

203
00:14:28.300 --> 00:14:31.630
Funkfreed that train can't
get here quick enough.

204
00:14:32.270 --> 00:14:34.270
Soon, I'll have enough power

205
00:14:34.300 --> 00:14:37.570
to bring the whole
world to its knees!

206
00:14:45.710 --> 00:14:48.270
[LUFFY]
Only one thing to do.

207
00:14:48.270 --> 00:14:51.370
We set off and rescue them right away!

208
00:14:51.800 --> 00:14:54.300
[ZORO]
I had a feeling you'd say that.

209
00:14:59.420 --> 00:15:01.880
Hey, help us out, Rope Guy.

210
00:15:02.130 --> 00:15:04.000
We need a boat.

211
00:15:04.030 --> 00:15:05.770
Actually, we need a sea train.

212
00:15:05.800 --> 00:15:07.640
Do you have another one of those?

213
00:15:07.640 --> 00:15:09.740
There is no "other" sea train.

214
00:15:09.770 --> 00:15:12.110
The Puffing Tom is one of a kind.

215
00:15:12.140 --> 00:15:14.480
The man who made that train's a legend.

216
00:15:14.510 --> 00:15:16.740
It's miracle it
got finished at all.

217
00:15:16.780 --> 00:15:20.410
So, sorry, I can't pull another
Sea Train out of my ass.

218
00:15:20.440 --> 00:15:22.320
Okay, then lend us a ship!

219
00:15:22.320 --> 00:15:24.820
The strongest and fastest
one you guys've got!

220
00:15:25.040 --> 00:15:27.840
[PAULIE]
Damn it, would you
give it a rest already?!

221
00:15:27.880 --> 00:15:29.010
Are you stupid?!

222
00:15:29.060 --> 00:15:31.030
You saw what just happened!

223
00:15:31.060 --> 00:15:32.930
You barely survived
that wave on land

224
00:15:32.970 --> 00:15:34.770
and you wanna go out to sea?!

225
00:15:34.800 --> 00:15:36.500
[WORKMAN]
I don't care how
good the ship is...

226
00:15:36.540 --> 00:15:37.740
you wouldn't last five minutes!

227
00:15:37.740 --> 00:15:38.440
You idiot!

228
00:15:38.440 --> 00:15:40.780
[PAULIE]
Even during a normal Aqua Laguna

229
00:15:40.810 --> 00:15:43.380
no ship has ever made
it through the storm.

230
00:15:43.410 --> 00:15:45.450
And this year, it's anything but normal.

231
00:15:45.480 --> 00:15:48.450
Just look at what happened
to the backstreets.

232
00:15:48.470 --> 00:15:52.540
This is the first time the waves have ever
done damage like that.

233
00:15:52.570 --> 00:15:54.570
Water Seven was built to last.

234
00:15:54.610 --> 00:15:57.440
If it starts shaking, then we damn well
better listen.

235
00:15:57.440 --> 00:15:59.320
I'm telling you,
even if you went out there

236
00:15:59.320 --> 00:16:02.420
in our biggest galleon,
you'd be smashed to smithereens.

237
00:16:02.450 --> 00:16:04.620
I'm not gonna let
you sail out there

238
00:16:04.720 --> 00:16:07.320
if I know you won't
make it back alive.

239
00:16:07.350 --> 00:16:09.390
Wait 'til morning.

240
00:16:10.360 --> 00:16:13.390
We'll lend you a ship as soon as the storm
passes.

241
00:16:13.430 --> 00:16:15.660
The rest of you head to the evacuation
shelter.

242
00:16:16.120 --> 00:16:18.000
We're done searching for missing people.

243
00:16:18.750 --> 00:16:21.250
Hold on.

244
00:16:21.280 --> 00:16:24.380
If we wait until
after the storm settles

245
00:16:24.420 --> 00:16:27.890
we won't make it in time
to save Robin, will we?

246
00:16:28.820 --> 00:16:32.460
I heard about Enies Lobby long before we
came here.

247
00:16:32.490 --> 00:16:34.230
When you said it was
a government island,

248
00:16:34.260 --> 00:16:35.800
it made me remember something.

249
00:16:35.830 --> 00:16:37.030
It's not just a base.

250
00:16:37.060 --> 00:16:40.530
It's also where the Gates of Justice are
located, isn't it?

251
00:16:41.330 --> 00:16:43.000
[ZORO]
Gates of Justice?

252
00:16:43.030 --> 00:16:46.070
Enies Lobby is known
as a "Judicial island."

253
00:16:46.100 --> 00:16:47.300
But that's all a lie.

254
00:16:47.330 --> 00:16:50.440
The court they have there is only for
show.

255
00:16:50.470 --> 00:16:52.440
The truth is, if
you've been taken there,

256
00:16:52.470 --> 00:16:55.180
then you're already
considered guilty.

257
00:16:55.210 --> 00:16:57.280
When you arrive the
government walks you

258
00:16:57.310 --> 00:16:59.550
through an empty courtroom,
leading to a pair of

259
00:16:59.570 --> 00:17:04.780
cold, steel doors that
tower above the entire island.

260
00:17:05.880 --> 00:17:08.920
Those doors are known as the Gates of
Justice.

261
00:17:09.280 --> 00:17:10.450
The criminals who
walk through them

262
00:17:10.480 --> 00:17:12.250
must abandon all hope.

263
00:17:12.280 --> 00:17:13.520
Once they reach the other side,

264
00:17:13.550 --> 00:17:16.190
they'll never see the
light of day again.

265
00:17:16.220 --> 00:17:17.960
Once you set sail
beyond those doors,

266
00:17:17.990 --> 00:17:20.220
there are only two
destinations you can reach.

267
00:17:20.260 --> 00:17:23.060
Neither of which you
are ever likely to leave.

268
00:17:24.570 --> 00:17:26.410
One is Navy Headquarters

269
00:17:26.440 --> 00:17:27.940
where the strongest
military powers

270
00:17:27.980 --> 00:17:31.240
in the world gather
in the name of justice.

271
00:17:31.650 --> 00:17:34.850
The other is Impel Down
an underwater prison,

272
00:17:34.880 --> 00:17:38.160
filled with torture chambers
and execution blocks.

273
00:17:38.190 --> 00:17:40.390
No matter how
vicious they may be,

274
00:17:40.420 --> 00:17:43.160
the criminals imprisoned
there can only wait for death.

275
00:17:44.230 --> 00:17:46.900
In other words
going to Enies Lobby

276
00:17:46.930 --> 00:17:49.300
is no different than
a death sentence.

277
00:17:49.330 --> 00:17:53.170
There's no trial, no justice
and no hope of escape.

278
00:17:53.200 --> 00:17:54.970
Am I right?

279
00:17:55.640 --> 00:17:57.760
[NAMI]
Robin has a bounty on her head.

280
00:17:58.150 --> 00:18:01.090
No matter where they take her,
she'll face death, or worse.

281
00:18:01.120 --> 00:18:02.490
Every second we
sit here talking,

282
00:18:02.520 --> 00:18:05.460
she gets one step closer
to the Gates of Justice.

283
00:18:05.490 --> 00:18:08.600
Don't you dare tell us to wait until
tomorrow!

284
00:18:11.100 --> 00:18:12.670
[PAULIE]
If you know that much already,

285
00:18:12.700 --> 00:18:14.870
I've only got one thing to say.

286
00:18:14.900 --> 00:18:17.300
Even if the sea was
calm and you were able

287
00:18:17.340 --> 00:18:21.040
to set sail that's the last
place you should ever go.

288
00:18:21.080 --> 00:18:22.310
Don't forget, you people are

289
00:18:22.340 --> 00:18:25.180
wanted criminals just
the same as your friend.

290
00:18:25.360 --> 00:18:27.690
Just like you said,
Enies Lobby is the front door

291
00:18:27.720 --> 00:18:30.360
to the World Government's
own personal playground.

292
00:18:30.390 --> 00:18:31.490
They've drawn battle lines

293
00:18:31.530 --> 00:18:34.630
around that place that
should never ever be crossed.

294
00:18:34.660 --> 00:18:37.500
Regardless of how they
feel about their crewmates,

295
00:18:37.530 --> 00:18:38.870
no pirate would be stupid enough

296
00:18:38.900 --> 00:18:41.170
to launch a
rescue mission there.

297
00:18:41.260 --> 00:18:43.190
They know what would happen.

298
00:18:43.310 --> 00:18:44.910
Picking a fight in that place

299
00:18:44.940 --> 00:18:48.610
is like declaring war
on the entire Navy!

300
00:18:52.450 --> 00:18:54.860
[WORKMAN]
Hey. I know how you must
feel, but Paulie's right!

301
00:18:54.890 --> 00:18:57.390
You can't leave during
Aqua Laguna, anyway!

302
00:18:57.560 --> 00:18:58.990
You'll be dead before you even get there!

303
00:18:58.990 --> 00:19:01.490
There's no point in throwing your lives
away over this!

304
00:19:02.390 --> 00:19:05.060
Luffy.

305
00:19:05.090 --> 00:19:06.600
[LUFFY]
Fine then.

306
00:19:06.600 --> 00:19:08.430
We'll steal a ship!

307
00:19:09.960 --> 00:19:12.600
Our crewmate is counting on us!

308
00:19:12.640 --> 00:19:15.760
[WORKMEN shouting]

309
00:19:16.260 --> 00:19:18.500
Don't try to get in our way!

310
00:19:18.530 --> 00:19:20.900
We're leaving now!

311
00:19:25.000 --> 00:19:27.500
[CHIMNEY]
Whoa, even the waves got mad!

312
00:19:30.620 --> 00:19:31.320
[WORKMAN]
Whoa!

313
00:19:31.320 --> 00:19:32.480
Is he gonna fight us?

314
00:19:32.520 --> 00:19:34.320
That sure was scary!

315
00:19:35.490 --> 00:19:36.390
Fine, then.

316
00:19:36.500 --> 00:19:38.630
You want a fight, you got it.

317
00:19:45.890 --> 00:19:46.920
[KOKORO]
All of you.

318
00:19:46.980 --> 00:19:48.540
Stop it!

319
00:19:50.630 --> 00:19:51.920
[NAMI]
Kokoro?

320
00:19:52.010 --> 00:19:54.880
Stop bein' such a
damn fool, Straw Hat.

321
00:19:55.780 --> 00:19:58.780
Like it or not, Paulie's right on this
one.

322
00:19:58.810 --> 00:20:01.350
Shut up granny,
it's none of your business!

323
00:20:01.380 --> 00:20:03.990
You sure about that, boy?

324
00:20:04.010 --> 00:20:06.040
Either way, these
folks are just trying

325
00:20:06.090 --> 00:20:08.790
to stop you from
killing yourself.

326
00:20:08.820 --> 00:20:11.730
The point is no
matter how mad you are,

327
00:20:11.750 --> 00:20:14.450
no ship can handle Aqua Laguna.

328
00:20:14.780 --> 00:20:18.450
Only a sea train made by a legendary man
stands a chance.

329
00:20:18.720 --> 00:20:20.690
I know that, but
I don't have any choice,

330
00:20:20.720 --> 00:20:24.600
since the only sea train in the
world has left town already!

331
00:20:25.750 --> 00:20:28.500
If you're prepared to die, then that's
fine.

332
00:20:29.000 --> 00:20:30.130
Just come along with me.

333
00:20:30.470 --> 00:20:33.740
We'll brave the storm on my sea train.

334
00:20:39.130 --> 00:20:42.510
<b>Car 7
(Last Car)</b>

335
00:20:51.440 --> 00:20:55.780
<b>Car 6
(Freight Car)</b>

336
00:20:59.890 --> 00:21:00.590
[OFFICIAL]
You idiots!

337
00:21:00.590 --> 00:21:01.790
Don't just stand there!

338
00:21:01.820 --> 00:21:05.930
If he's not wearing a uniform,
then he must be an intruder!

339
00:21:09.500 --> 00:21:11.080
Get him!

340
00:21:11.460 --> 00:21:15.460
[OFFICIALS]
I guess playing innocent doesn't work in
here.

341
00:21:15.920 --> 00:21:19.260
[OFFICIALS groaning]

342
00:21:24.480 --> 00:21:27.420
And here I thought I could get out of a
fight.

343
00:21:27.420 --> 00:21:29.990
Oh well, it's not my funeral.

344
00:21:32.650 --> 00:21:34.490
[USOPP]
Sanji?!

345
00:21:34.520 --> 00:21:36.060
[BOSSES]
– Hold it!
– Hold it!

346
00:21:39.330 --> 00:21:42.600
You think we're gonna let you get away
with that?

347
00:21:42.630 --> 00:21:44.600
If you're smart.

348
00:21:48.130 --> 00:21:50.130
[clicking tongue]

349
00:21:50.610 --> 00:21:56.440
[SANJI]
Collier Frite!

350
00:22:03.390 --> 00:22:04.660
Wait, you didn't
hijack the Sea Train

351
00:22:04.690 --> 00:22:07.230
just to rescue me, did you?

352
00:22:07.260 --> 00:22:10.230
I don't even know what you're doing here.

353
00:22:11.680 --> 00:22:13.680
[lighter igniting]

354
00:22:16.100 --> 00:22:17.470
Also, what's your name again,

355
00:22:17.500 --> 00:22:20.040
I don't believe we've actually met before,
have we?

356
00:22:20.070 --> 00:22:21.380
Oh, are you kidding me?

357
00:22:21.410 --> 00:22:23.910
You jerk.

358
00:22:25.450 --> 00:22:26.150
Bingo!

359
00:22:26.150 --> 00:22:28.180
Transponder snails!

360
00:22:28.280 --> 00:22:29.310
Hmm, okay.

361
00:22:29.350 --> 00:22:32.180
This must be a communications
room or something.

362
00:22:32.220 --> 00:22:35.550
Lucky I ran into this place so soon.

363
00:22:35.580 --> 00:22:37.090
Those guys I beat
up in the last cart

364
00:22:37.120 --> 00:22:38.620
only had a bunch
of useless crap.

365
00:22:38.660 --> 00:22:40.560
Masks and
costumes and stuff.

366
00:22:40.590 --> 00:22:44.060
Anyway, now that I have this
I can get in touch with Nami.

367
00:22:44.090 --> 00:22:44.880
[FRANKY]
Let me guess.

368
00:22:44.880 --> 00:22:47.180
He's one of your pirate friends,
isn't he?

369
00:22:47.210 --> 00:22:48.350
[SANJI and USOPP]
– EX friend.
– EX friend.

370
00:22:48.380 --> 00:22:50.320
The question is, who are you?

371
00:22:50.350 --> 00:22:52.980
I'm the face of Water Seven's underworld.

372
00:22:53.120 --> 00:22:55.170
The ship dismantler, Franky.

373
00:22:55.170 --> 00:22:57.770
So you're the bastard who beat up Usopp,
huh?

374
00:22:59.720 --> 00:23:00.590
He may be dead to me now,

375
00:23:00.660 --> 00:23:03.190
but he was part of
our crew, back then!

376
00:23:03.220 --> 00:23:05.630
[SANJI]
How many pieces you
want me to cut you into?

377
00:23:05.670 --> 00:23:07.370
[USOPP]
No, no, no, wait, wait, wait.

378
00:23:07.400 --> 00:23:10.570
It's not like that now, a lot
of stuff has changed since then!

379
00:23:10.620 --> 00:23:11.790
Hey, punk!

380
00:23:11.820 --> 00:23:13.720
You're lucky I'm tied up!

381
00:23:13.760 --> 00:23:16.260
C'mon man, that
line's getting old.

382
00:23:16.290 --> 00:23:17.630
Seriously, he's a good guy.

383
00:23:17.660 --> 00:23:20.730
He saved the Merry
at least for a while.

384
00:23:20.760 --> 00:23:21.930
Oh yeah.

385
00:23:24.090 --> 00:23:26.380
The Merry was...

386
00:23:27.420 --> 00:23:28.550
Whoa.

387
00:23:28.580 --> 00:23:31.690
C'mon buddy, you can't get
all sad n' mopey on me now!

388
00:23:31.880 --> 00:23:33.750
Hey! Blondie! Untie me!

389
00:23:33.780 --> 00:23:36.180
Pretty Please?

390
00:23:36.230 --> 00:23:37.260
You can spend the
rest of your life

391
00:23:37.300 --> 00:23:39.670
in that potato
sack for all I care!

392
00:23:39.700 --> 00:23:40.870
Screw you!

393
00:23:40.900 --> 00:23:43.600
I said "pretty please" what
the hell else do you want?!

394
00:23:43.640 --> 00:23:44.800
Stop it!

395
00:23:44.840 --> 00:23:46.270
No more fighting, guys!

396
00:23:46.310 --> 00:23:47.370
Look!

397
00:23:47.410 --> 00:23:50.410
If we keep yelling, then the
marine's are gonna come!

398
00:23:50.440 --> 00:23:51.910
[FRANKY]
Yeah? Then shut up!

399
00:23:51.940 --> 00:23:52.610
[USOPP]
Say what?!

400
00:23:52.610 --> 00:23:53.260
[FRANKY]
Whatever!

401
00:23:53.260 --> 00:23:54.560
Just untie me, okay?

402
00:23:54.590 --> 00:23:55.400
[SANJI]
Don't order me around!

403
00:23:55.430 --> 00:23:57.660
[USOPP]
Stop fighting already!

404
00:23:57.950 --> 00:23:59.950
[rumbling]

405
00:24:01.760 --> 00:24:02.460
Captain T-Bone?

406
00:24:02.460 --> 00:24:03.960
What are you...?

407
00:24:07.170 --> 00:24:08.370
A secret base?!

408
00:24:08.410 --> 00:24:12.340
It's been more than 8 years
since anyone's set foot in here.

409
00:24:11.680 --> 00:24:16.230
<b>Red Brick Warehouse
Behind the Waste Facility</b>

410
00:24:12.380 --> 00:24:16.250
And nobody's touched the
sea train for more than 12.

411
00:24:16.230 --> 00:24:17.480
[LUFFY]
Let's go, Chopper!

412
00:24:17.680 --> 00:24:18.720
Right!

413
00:24:18.750 --> 00:24:21.890
I'm warning you, the thing
might not run anymore!

414
00:24:21.890 --> 00:24:22.550
What?

415
00:24:22.550 --> 00:24:23.890
You better be kidding me!

416
00:24:27.960 --> 00:24:30.360
Now now, settle down, boys.

417
00:24:30.480 --> 00:24:31.980
You can run as fast as you like,

418
00:24:32.020 --> 00:24:35.250
but you're not getting
inside without the key!

419
00:24:35.290 --> 00:24:36.220
Huh?

420
00:24:36.310 --> 00:24:37.980
Now that's weird.

421
00:24:38.040 --> 00:24:40.380
It's open-

422
00:24:42.850 --> 00:24:44.250
Whoa-hoa!

423
00:24:44.280 --> 00:24:45.520
Awesome!

424
00:24:45.550 --> 00:24:47.820
Check out the face!

425
00:24:49.020 --> 00:24:51.990
[CHOPPER]
It's so cool!

426
00:24:52.020 --> 00:24:55.960
[KOKORO]
Unlike the Puffing Tom, this one here's a
crazy train.

427
00:24:55.990 --> 00:24:58.400
Its name is "Rocketman."

428
00:24:58.420 --> 00:25:02.190
Comes with no guarantees, so board at your
own risk.

429
00:25:02.220 --> 00:25:03.130
Rocketman!

430
00:25:03.160 --> 00:25:04.360
Sounds fast!

431
00:25:04.400 --> 00:25:06.040
Neat-o!

432
00:25:07.400 --> 00:25:09.040
Did you have to add the face?

433
00:25:09.070 --> 00:25:12.240
Don't worry, it may be mean, but it won't
bite.

434
00:25:15.180 --> 00:25:17.450
Hey look, it's Ice Pops!

435
00:25:17.480 --> 00:25:19.150
[ICEBURG]
Hello there, Straw Hat.

436
00:25:19.370 --> 00:25:20.830
So you're okay after all.

437
00:25:21.050 --> 00:25:23.820
It seems your friend's faith was
well-founded.

438
00:25:23.860 --> 00:25:25.590
I assume you brought them here,
Kokoro?

439
00:25:25.610 --> 00:25:28.380
The question is, what are you doing here?

440
00:25:28.410 --> 00:25:31.210
You've been through a
lot today, you need rest!

441
00:25:31.250 --> 00:25:33.120
Mmwell let's just say you

442
00:25:33.150 --> 00:25:35.250
and I were thinking
the same thing.

443
00:25:35.920 --> 00:25:38.820
We have a soft spot for idiots,
don't we?

444
00:25:43.900 --> 00:25:44.600
Go ahead.

445
00:25:45.150 --> 00:25:46.940
I just finished servicing it.

446
00:25:46.940 --> 00:25:49.940
Water and coal have been loaded and the
steam's building up now.

447
00:25:50.950 --> 00:25:53.570
[LUFFY]
Thanks for getting it ready
for us, we owe you one!

448
00:25:56.230 --> 00:25:58.160
I wouldn't celebrate
yet, if I were you.

449
00:25:58.200 --> 00:26:00.370
You might not even survive the ride.

450
00:26:00.450 --> 00:26:03.590
This was our failed prototype before we
made the Puffing Tom.

451
00:26:03.620 --> 00:26:06.420
No matter how you tune it, you can't
control its speed.

452
00:26:06.460 --> 00:26:10.260
In other words, it's a runaway train.

453
00:26:10.260 --> 00:26:11.360
That's fine!

454
00:26:11.390 --> 00:26:13.320
It can go as fast as it wants!

455
00:26:16.200 --> 00:26:18.360
Hurry up, let's go!

456
00:26:18.520 --> 00:26:20.060
Get on already!

457
00:26:20.890 --> 00:26:23.390
We're leaving as soon as Nami gets here,
Granny!

458
00:26:26.470 --> 00:26:27.170
Ah man.

459
00:26:27.170 --> 00:26:29.040
[CHOPPER]
Luffy, are you okay?

460
00:26:29.320 --> 00:26:31.890
You've been kinda shaky on
your feet since we found you.

461
00:26:32.030 --> 00:26:33.660
[ZORO]
He probably just lost too much blood.

462
00:26:34.290 --> 00:26:35.360
Maybe.

463
00:26:35.390 --> 00:26:37.650
I am feeling kinda dizzy.

464
00:26:37.650 --> 00:26:39.620
I think I need some meat.

465
00:26:39.650 --> 00:26:42.320
[NAMI]
Hurry, this way!

466
00:26:42.360 --> 00:26:44.360
[STATION ATTENDANTS gasping]

467
00:26:44.420 --> 00:26:45.120
[STATION ATTENDANT]
Wait!

468
00:26:45.120 --> 00:26:46.090
I don't see why you have to go

469
00:26:46.110 --> 00:26:48.250
all the way down here
just to eat your dinner!

470
00:26:48.260 --> 00:26:49.100
He's right!

471
00:26:49.110 --> 00:26:50.480
If you're hungry, eat now!

472
00:26:50.480 --> 00:26:52.140
[NAMI]
You think all that food is for me?!

473
00:26:52.200 --> 00:26:53.270
What?!

474
00:26:53.300 --> 00:26:54.870
Sorry I took so long!

475
00:26:54.910 --> 00:26:55.740
Nami.

476
00:26:55.780 --> 00:26:57.880
Hey, save the
small talk for later!

477
00:26:57.910 --> 00:27:00.250
Get on board so we can go!

478
00:27:00.320 --> 00:27:01.660
Wow, amazing!

479
00:27:01.930 --> 00:27:03.390
So there's another
sea train huh?

480
00:27:03.760 --> 00:27:07.430
It was hiding here all
this time and we never knew!

481
00:27:07.460 --> 00:27:08.700
[STATION ATTENDANT]
This is a real surprise!

482
00:27:08.790 --> 00:27:10.660
You're the one who
told us we have to hurry.

483
00:27:10.660 --> 00:27:12.770
Why are you the
last one to get here!

484
00:27:13.110 --> 00:27:14.450
And what's with that big bag?

485
00:27:14.610 --> 00:27:16.380
I brought you food and drinks.

486
00:27:16.410 --> 00:27:18.010
I'm sorry I just yelled at you.

487
00:27:19.580 --> 00:27:21.050
[KOKORO]
He's ready to go!

488
00:27:21.130 --> 00:27:23.440
[ICEBURG]
You'll shoot out of the canal into the
ocean.

489
00:27:23.470 --> 00:27:25.150
If you can latch onto
the railway after that,

490
00:27:25.150 --> 00:27:26.490
it should be a good start.

491
00:27:26.710 --> 00:27:28.040
Don't you worry a bit!

492
00:27:28.370 --> 00:27:31.310
I like to drink,
but I take my job seriously!

493
00:27:31.340 --> 00:27:32.240
You just stay here

494
00:27:32.280 --> 00:27:34.310
and give that body
of yours a good rest!

495
00:27:34.340 --> 00:27:35.340
Sounds fine to me.

496
00:27:35.380 --> 00:27:37.450
And while I'm taking
care of these pirate folk,

497
00:27:37.480 --> 00:27:40.450
I hope you don't mind watching
Gonbe and Chimney for me.

498
00:27:43.100 --> 00:27:46.480
[ZAMBAI]
Straw Hat!

499
00:27:48.240 --> 00:27:50.040
[LUFFY]
Who's there?

500
00:27:50.520 --> 00:27:52.030
The Franky Family!

501
00:27:56.110 --> 00:27:58.180
We're kind of busy right now.

502
00:27:58.210 --> 00:28:00.110
Please! Straw Hat.

503
00:28:00.160 --> 00:28:02.500
You guys gotta take us with you!

504
00:28:02.550 --> 00:28:04.220
The people from Galley-La said

505
00:28:04.250 --> 00:28:08.060
you were gonna take a
sea train to Enies Lobby!

506
00:28:08.100 --> 00:28:10.100
Those government bastards took Franky!

507
00:28:10.200 --> 00:28:12.870
They took our bro away from us!

508
00:28:12.950 --> 00:28:13.850
We wanna go,

509
00:28:13.920 --> 00:28:16.930
but we can't get through
Aqua Laguna alone!

510
00:28:16.960 --> 00:28:19.530
You sure you wanna pick a fight on their
turf?

511
00:28:19.560 --> 00:28:21.500
I'll fight anyone, anywhere!

512
00:28:21.510 --> 00:28:23.350
[FAMILY MAN]
We gotta get our bro back!

513
00:28:23.670 --> 00:28:24.700
I don't care what happens

514
00:28:24.730 --> 00:28:26.940
to us as long as
we can save him!

515
00:28:27.030 --> 00:28:28.660
[KIWI]
We're begging you!

516
00:28:28.740 --> 00:28:30.710
Please help us, Straw Hat!

517
00:28:30.740 --> 00:28:32.780
We'll do anything!

518
00:28:33.200 --> 00:28:36.040
[FAMILY MAN]
If we don't hurry, bro is done for!

519
00:28:36.040 --> 00:28:37.950
You've gotta be kidding me.

520
00:28:37.980 --> 00:28:43.180
You steal our money, beat up our
friend, then ask us for help?!

521
00:28:47.890 --> 00:28:50.590
I don't care.

522
00:28:50.590 --> 00:28:53.890
Even if it's wrong,
I'm still begging you.

523
00:28:53.910 --> 00:28:57.640
I'll give up my pride if I can save him!

524
00:29:11.420 --> 00:29:12.560
C'mon.

525
00:29:12.590 --> 00:29:13.930
Hurry up!

526
00:29:15.240 --> 00:29:17.240
[EVERYONE cheering]

527
00:29:18.420 --> 00:29:19.820
Thank you so much.

528
00:29:20.390 --> 00:29:23.420
Are you sure about this?!

529
00:29:23.450 --> 00:29:24.950
Eh, it's fine.

530
00:29:25.490 --> 00:29:26.910
[ZAMBAI]
Thank you.

531
00:29:27.970 --> 00:29:29.940
Thanks, Straw Hat.

532
00:29:30.460 --> 00:29:32.600
Well, let's go!

533
00:29:32.630 --> 00:29:36.660
Ah we don't have to
get on the train, though.

534
00:29:36.660 --> 00:29:37.740
We'll just hop on our king bulls

535
00:29:37.740 --> 00:29:40.910
and head out to sea the
same time the train takes off.

536
00:29:40.940 --> 00:29:43.980
All you gotta do is let the
bulls catch a ride on your tail.

537
00:29:44.220 --> 00:29:45.720
What're king bulls?

538
00:29:45.880 --> 00:29:47.450
Anyway, we're off!

539
00:29:47.450 --> 00:29:48.010
Thanks!

540
00:29:48.010 --> 00:29:49.240
See ya, soon!

541
00:29:49.770 --> 00:29:51.270
Let's go!

542
00:29:51.370 --> 00:29:53.840
[FAMILY MEN]
– Yeah!
– Yeah!

543
00:30:00.430 --> 00:30:02.440
Let's show those bastards

544
00:30:02.440 --> 00:30:05.140
what we're made
of and save our bro!

545
00:30:05.180 --> 00:30:06.410
We're comin', bro!

546
00:30:07.560 --> 00:30:11.560
[CHOPPER grunting]

547
00:30:14.580 --> 00:30:16.510
How's that?

548
00:30:18.040 --> 00:30:18.740
Good!

549
00:30:18.740 --> 00:30:20.480
Now let's take off!

550
00:30:20.900 --> 00:30:24.400
[train whistle]

551
00:30:55.740 --> 00:30:57.740
[coughing]

552
00:30:58.470 --> 00:31:00.910
All right boys and girls.

553
00:31:00.940 --> 00:31:03.670
Hold on tight,
so you don't fall off!

554
00:31:15.720 --> 00:31:18.680
[KOKORO]
Now Departing Water
Seven for Enies Lobby!

555
00:31:18.680 --> 00:31:21.580
Here comes Rocketman!

556
00:31:25.650 --> 00:31:26.980
Yeah!

557
00:31:27.020 --> 00:31:28.820
Full speed!

558
00:31:28.860 --> 00:31:30.860
[train whistle]

559
00:31:32.250 --> 00:31:33.290
Let's go!

560
00:31:33.560 --> 00:31:36.930
We'll get it all back!
